{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation Bias: The model consistently forecasts a flat, mean-reverting trajectory (approx. 68-69 EUR) while true prices exhibit strong upward momentum, frequently exceeding 75 EUR. Apply a persistent upward bias correction of +5 to +8 EUR to all forecast horizons.",
    "Lag in Spike Response: The model fails to capture the magnitude of price spikes (e.g., the rise from ~66 to ~76 EUR). When sentiment history shows a sequence of 1.00 (positive) following a dip, immediately adjust the forecast upward by at least 10% rather than relying on the model's slow drift.",
    "Overshoot Correction on Dips: The model underestimates the depth of corrections but overestimates the speed of recovery. When true prices drop below 70 EUR, do not revert to the model's ~68 EUR baseline; instead, assume a higher floor near 71-72 EUR before the next rally.",
    "Sentiment-Weighted Volatility: High sentiment scores (1.00) correlate with large upward jumps (3-5 EUR/day) that the model misses entirely. Multiply the model's daily change by a factor of 2.5 when sentiment is 1.00, and by 0.5 when sentiment is 0.00.",
    "Horizon-Specific Drift: The error gap widens significantly after day 5. For forecasts beyond the 10-day horizon, apply a linear trend adjustment based on the last 5 days of true price momentum rather than the model's static mean."
  ]
}
